--TEST--
`queryAs<T>` names the class a row is built into, so a scalar written there is refused where a `Core\Db\Row` reader would have been the answer — `rule:core-classes/derive-field-list`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/derive-field-list`: hydrating is an ordinary `new`, so the type argument has to be
// something there is a constructor for. `queryAs<int>` reads as "one column per
// row" and is not what this member does — `$rows->column()` and `$row->int()`
// are the members for reading a column, and both come off the `Rows<Row>` that
// `query` already answers.
use Core\Db\Derive;

#[Derive]
class Person {
    public uint $id;

    public function constructor(uint $id)
    {
        $this->id = $id;
    }
}

// The same member on the other half of `Core\Db\Queryable`, written the way
// § 18 asks for: a class, so there is something to construct.
class People {
    public static function everyone(Core\Db\Transaction $tx): Core\Db\Rows<Person>
    {
        return $tx->queryAs<Person>("select id from people", []);
    }
}

var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

var $rows = $db->queryAs<int>("select id from people", []);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0465]: `Core\Db\Connection::queryAs` builds a class or an inline shape, or a list of one, and `int` is none of those
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
